Z||000000||Verticalspeed||02-18-2001||10:45 AM||||So I had been having the "wobble" tire-out-of-balance syndrome for a few weeks. Took the tires in to Discount Tires twice to have them balanced. The problem got worse!! I took the tires to a different branch and they told me that my tires were "way off" by 2.50 ounces, and the weights were incorrect!!!! After they "took a little" time to balance them right, the car rides normal again...Except I think I blew my front left wheel bearings because I hear this screeching noise from in there, and there is grease all over the spindle nut area! Do you think my inner-outter bearings are shot? They are only $14 at autozone. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FIERO1985||02-18-2001||10:18 PM||||I work at discount tire and sometimes that will occur; a inexpeirienced tech will put the wrong weights or not care about the customer and the wheel out of balance! A good thing to do if they still cause vibrations is to request the load variance balance from them and if that dont work you have more problems than out of balance wheels<P>Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
